    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0590" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to
                        Prime Minister Churchill
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d327-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent-priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-02">January 2, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret for the Former Naval
                        Person from the President No. 252. Your 251: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>I heartily approve your Paragraph One.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The aliases from this end will be (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) Don
                            Quixote and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) Sancho Panza.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>No press correspondents. I will bring one Navy Photographer and we can
                            join in joint release.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>I honestly think de Gaulle would feel happier if he postponed visit
                            until after “<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                    >Symbol</hi>”. Also I would find great difficulty in
                            giving him any time even if he were to leave at once.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d327-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d327-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
